      {
        "id": 53471,
        "name": "Amnachaidh",
        "username": "Amnachaidh",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/ba8739/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-02-26T12:36:19.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>As I understand it, \"Discarding a card\" refers to a card going from your hand to the trash</p><p>\"Destroying a card\" refers to a card going from in play to the trash.</p><p>Off hand, I can't think of an effect that takes a card entirely off the table.&nbsp; Some cards, like Haka's Savage Mana, may make the card inaccessible to its deck, but it's stil out there.</p><p>That was many words to say, \"Your last possibiity is correct\".</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:27:39.883Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
