        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>As I understand it, &quot;Discarding a card&quot; refers to a card going from your hand to the trash</p><p>&quot;Destroying a card&quot; refers to a card going from in play to the trash.</p><p>Off hand, I can&#39;t think of an effect that takes a card entirely off the table.&nbsp; Some cards, like Haka&#39;s Savage Mana, may make the card inaccessible to its deck, but it&#39;s stil out there.</p><p>That was many words to say, &quot;Your last possibiity is correct&quot;.</p>",
