        "id": 53473,
        "name": "fba827",
        "username": "fba827",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/b9bd4f/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-02-26T20:40:55.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>As said above, destroying a card means to put it in the trash pile for its deck.&nbsp; Only an in-play card can be destroyed (rather than one from your hand, as taking a card from your hand and putting it in the trash is discarding)</p><p>Certain hero/villain/environment cards will trigger an effect when a card is destroyed which is why they call it 'destroying' rather than simply saying 'put it in your trash'</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:27:40.036Z",
